## Cross-cutting Concerns

**Authorization**: Both new API routes rely solely on authentication (any logged-in user can read/delete any fixed worklog by ID or lot O2I). If the application has collaborator-scoped access (e.g., a PM can only see their own lots), an ownership check against `event.context.user` should be added to the DELETE route at minimum.

**Error propagation — `save()` partial failure**: The slideover emits `saved` and closes regardless of whether all deletions succeeded. This means the parent refreshes but the user may not realize some items survived. A stricter flow would only emit `saved` + close on full success.

**Dead code in `useUo`**: `deleteFixedWorklog` and `deleteFixedWorklogs` exported from `useUo` are not consumed anywhere outside the composable. They should be removed or consolidated with `useFixedWorklogs`.

